  {
   "id": "fischer-mechanism-note",
   "type": "textlabel",
   "x": 620,
   "y": 140,
   "rot": 0,
   "label": "",
   "showLabel": false,
   "params": {
    "text": "### Reported mechanism\n- Distinct ~810 nm excitation and 532 nm depletion\n- Both AOM-gated at 4 kHz and 3% duty\n- Central π zone covers 50% **pupil area**\n  (meridional diameter = √0.5)\n- One circularly polarized, NA 1.4 focus\n\nThe pupil step gives axial lobes **and** a radial ring.\nIt is not a vortex doughnut.\n\n**Computed:** rays, gates, polarization, relay, focus,\npupil clipping and sample hits.\n\n**Not computed:** stimulated depletion, vectorial PSF,\ntriplet dynamics, resin kinetics or calibrated curing.",
    "fontSize": 8,
    "fill": "#334155"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "fischer-controls-note",
   "type": "textlabel",
   "x": 620,
   "y": 282,
   "rot": 0,
   "label": "",
   "showLabel": false,
   "params": {
    "text": "### Controls\n1. Disable **532 nm depletion** → green path off.\n2. Set **pupil area** or **OPD** to 0 → mask off;\n   geometric focus unchanged (diffraction unsupported).\n3. Set stage to **Static** → scan and sweep stop.\n4. Disable **810 nm excitation** → no voxel arrivals.\n\n*Free interpretation — not specified in the paper:*\n80 MHz, 150 fs, 10.48 mW excitation; beam size;\nrelay lenses; fold/combiner; EFL/WD/oil; scan travel; dump.\nConfigured-value handoff is off; use the paper page.",
    "fontSize": 8,
    "fill": "#334155"
   }
